.cljc` | 422 | `repl.cljc:28, :232`, `linker.cljc:49, :2171, :2462`, `publish.cljc:10, :161` | 37 files (every test that builds a stack kernel through `dl/adapt`; the 10 C4 files among them) | delete after 8c |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:42:| `yin.vm.ucf.handoff` (old transport, versions 0/1/2, `export-task` `:1392`, `resume-task` `:3778`, `codec-versions` `:3253`) | `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc` | 3783 | none | 15 files: `handoff_test`, `handoff_v1_test`, `handoff_v2_{authority,census,custody,gates,holder,layout,test,validity,values,walker}`, `checkpoint_test`, `lift_v1_test`, `scalar_round_trip_test`, `ucf/safepoint_harness_test`, `lift_support`, `v2_support`; C4: `int_heap_test.cljc:241` (`export-task`), `int_contract_test.cljc:483` (`resume-task`) | delete (Q2) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:79:- **C4 track (10, owner question Q1):** `yang/python/antlr/{e2e_c2_test.clj, e2e_test.clj, float_address_test, int_contract_test, int_heap_test, int_literal_test, int_ops_test, linked_harness, prelude_parity_test, safepoint_test}` and `linked_harness.cljc:105-120` which binds `:semantic` to `linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program` and `:stack`/`:register` to `dl/adapt`/`rc/adapt`.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:97:| `manifest-golden` `b9dbaeff…` | `yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc:223-235` | py manifest address (JVM golden) | regenerate (C4 file, Q1) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:98:| `pysp-manifest-golden` `0971cc1e…` | `linked_safepoint_test.cljc:240-247` | pysp manifest | regenerate (C4 file, Q1) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:99:| 5 + 1 segment addresses | `int_literal_test.cljc` (5), `float_address_test.cljc:227-269` (1 + 4 fragments) | A addresses of Python literals under the OLD v3 vector? To verify at 8f: if these are tree or v4 addresses they hold; if v3 vector addresses they die with v3 | verify, regenerate only if they are v3 (C4 files, Q1) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:113:| `export-task`/`resume-task` | `handoff.cljc:1392, :3778` | the above + `int_heap_test.cljc:241`, `int_contract_test.cljc:483` (C4) | delete; the two C4 calls move to the holder path (`yin.vm.ucf.holder.export`/`driver`) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:158:- Docs that must change: the 13 files above; `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` (836 lines, describes the v3 machine; 25 citers including `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`, `repl.cljc`, `ucf.cljc`, `docs/agents/format.md`); `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (new revision record for `\"v4\"` as the one semantic contract); `yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:190, :390, :651, :3225, :3347` (phase-8 forward references); `yin.vm.linker.md:222-224` (§3 amendment); `yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.targets.md` (SHA-256 prose, lowerer names); `semantic-register-vm.md` status header `:1-11` (\"working name… takes the name `yin.vm.semantic`\"); `derivations.md` §7.4-§8.3 PROPOSED to DECIDED/DONE; `continuation.md` §8.4; `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` if any lane names change (none expected).\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:166:**Q1 (OWNER). Who edits the 10 C4 files, and when.** The cutover cannot compile without rewriting `linked_harness.cljc:105-120` and the ten Python tests that require the old kernel, `dl`, `rc` and `handoff`, and without regenerating `manifest-golden`, `pysp-manifest-golden` and verifying the literal-address pins. Options: (a) this track edits them in slice 8f under a frozen C4 branch state the owner declares (the other orchestrator pauses commits to those files for the slice's duration); (b) the other orchestrator ports them against a published 8c/8e API on a C4 branch, and 8f merges both. Recommendation: (a), because the change is mechanical (the harness's three backend lambdas and the loader) and a two-party edit of one file is the worst conflict shape; cost half a day plus the C4 slow lane (hours on a laptop; shiva/jupiter preferred). The owner must also say whether the C4 goldens are \"ours to move\" (derivations §8.1 says publish twice and diff; the review must show the diff).\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:178:**Q7. The old harness and stage tests of the old kernel.** `engine_gate_test`, `semantic_engine_test`, `semantic_ffi_test`, `semantic_stream_observer_test`, `stream_poll_test`, `telemetry_test`, `heap_reclamation_test` etc. exercise the engine through the old kernel. Recommendation: port, do not delete; the new kernel is the same engine's client. Slice 8f carries a coverage audit: list every deftest in deleted files, and for each name a surviving deftest or write one. Reviewer gate: the suite's deftest count after 8f is at least today's minus the 85 + 141 + (91 - ported) that are tests of deleted code, documented in the slice report with the list. Cost: in 8f's 2 days.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:180:**Q8. Who regenerates the C4 goldens and the literal-address pins.** Covered by Q1; the mechanical check is derivations §8.1 row 6 (publish twice, diff the manifest map). If the five `int_literal_test` and `float_address_test` pins are v3 vector addresses they die; if tree or v4 addresses they hold. Decided at 8f by printing them.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:182:**Q9. Deletion order (irreversible).** Fixed by this plan: 8a pins and regenerates goldens and moves the H descriptor golden; 8b moves BLAKE3; 8c switches production callers; 8d deletes the old transport; 8e deletes the three old lowerers; 8f deletes the old kernel and renames; 8g documents. Nothing is deleted before its replacement is green on three hosts in the same slice or earlier.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:184:**Q10. `derive_test`'s `:old` oracle legs** (`:150-160`, `:438-447`, `:612-630` `c4-backends :stack-old/:register-old`). These compare new lowerings against the old lowerers and die with them (8e). The execution oracle then compares `:stack-new`/`:register-new` against the walker and the semantic kernel only (§6.1 already names the walker as oracle). Recommendation: accept; the old lowerers' answers are already pinned as the §6.3 goldens.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:190:Estimates: codex implementation days; review rounds 2-4 per slice (Fable/opus, non-author). Hosts: every slice runs the quick tier on JVM per iteration (`bb test:sub:clj yin.vm` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`), `bb test:changed` on three hosts at landing (G2). Slow tier (`bb test:all`), C4 suite with `--slow`, and three hosts once at the phase boundary (8f/8g).\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:197:| **8d Old transport out** | delete `handoff.cljc`, `checkpoint.cljc`, 15 test files, `lift_support.cljc`, `v2_support.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`, 3 fixtures + minter; first move borrowed helpers into `rows_support.cljc` (new `frame_test`, `layout_test`, `semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test` requires rewired); `int_heap_test.cljc:241`, `int_contract_test.cljc:483` to the holder path (C4 files: Q1) | none (can run concurrently with 8ab/8c) | `rows-test/*`, `rows-checkpoint-test/*`, `compose-rows-test/*` (41), `fencing-rows-test`, `stage-e-rows-test`, `stage_e_process_test`, `holder/*`, `authority/*`, `semantic-register/safepoint-harness-test/*` (26), `frame-test/*` (10), `layout-test/*` (12); one new refusal row for a version-0/2 header | 3 | 1.5 d | 2-3 |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:198:| **8e Old lowerers out** | delete `debruijn_resolve.cljc`, `debruijn_linearize.cljc`, `debruijn_register_compile.cljc`, their 3 tests, `debruijn_register_benchmark_test`; port the contract facts of `debruijn_vm_contract_test`/`debruijn_register_contract_test` to `debruijn_code_test`/`debruijn_register_code_test`, delete the rest; `test_utils.cljc:24, :200-210` (`resolved-of` becomes `derive` over the projected vector); `derive_test` `:old` legs out (Q10); every test that builds a kernel through `dl/adapt`/`rc/adapt` (37 files, the 10 C4 files among them: Q1) switches to `derive/stack-image`/`register-image` over `(:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))` | 8c (production no longer calls them) | the full `yin.vm` subsystem quick tier; `derive-test/*` incl. `c4-execution-oracle` (`--slow`); `debruijn/register_test`, `debruijn/stack_*_test`; kondo clean (`clj -M:kondo`) with no unresolved namespace | 3 | 2 d | 2-3 |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:199:| **8f Old kernel out, rename, C4 gate** | delete `semantic.cljc`, `linearize.cljc`, `code.cljc` (what remains after 8c) and `semantic_test`, `linearize_test`, `code_test`; port `semantic_engine_test`, `semantic_ffi_test`, `semantic_stream_observer_test` to the new kernel; commit 1 `git mv` `semantic_register*` to `semantic*` and `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/` to `test/yin/vm/semantic/`; commit 2 rewrite the 56 requirers (`vm-load-program` to `load-ast`/`load-vector`); demos (`continuation_handoff.cljc`, `continuation_stream.cljs`, `register_bench_cljd.cljd`, `yin_vm_bench`) ported; `linked_harness.cljc:105-120`; C4 goldens regenerated and literal pins verified (Q1, Q8); coverage audit list | 8c, 8d, 8e | **phase gate**: `bb test:all` three hosts (slow tier), `bb test:sub yang.python --slow` (C4 suite: `import_test`, `linked_prelude_test`, `linked_safepoint_test`, `safepoint_test`, `dht_import_test`, `e2e_test`, `e2e_c2_test`, `prelude_parity_test`) over newly published images = the install-child gate of derivations §6.1.4 (c); `repl-test/*`, `dht_process_test`, `store_write_audit_test` (allowlist touches); deftest-count audit per Q7; kondo clean; `lib/cljd-out` cleaned before the Dart lane | 3 + shiva/jupiter for the slow tier | 3 d | 3-4 |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:200:| **8g Documentation** | the 13 design docs, `yin.vm.semantic.md` fate (Q6), `ucf-revisions.md` record, `linker.md` §3, `build-n-test.md` if needed, the frozen design's §10 item 8 marked complete, `derivations.md` §7.4-8.3 and `continuation.md` §8.4 statuses, `debruijn.*.md` SHA-256 prose | 8f | Architect doc review; `grep -r 'yin.vm.semantic-register' docs src test` returns only historical/dated statements; `grep -rn 'sha256' src/cljc/yin/vm` returns none | n/a | 1.5 d | 2 |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:210:| 8f | 8c, 8d, 8e | nothing |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:211:| 8g | 8f | nothing (docs only; may start drafting during 8f review) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:213:Gate list: quick tier (`bb test:sub:clj yin.vm` per iteration, `bb test:changed` three hosts at landing) for every slice; `bb test:sub yin.vm yin.vm.ucf` at 8c and 8e checkpoints; the slow tier once at 8f on shiva/jupiter plus the C4 suite with `--slow`; three hosts at every landing from 8ab up because the regenerated constants must agree on JVM, Node and Dart (that is what `pinned-identities-are-host-independent` and `register-determinism` exist for).\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:221:1. **Mass rename collides with the other orchestrator.** 56 files, 10 of them C4's, and `linked_harness.cljc` is the shared hinge. Mitigation: Q1 ruling; freeze window announced via collab/owner relay before 8e starts; 8e and 8f edit C4 files only as mechanical API substitution with no behavioural change; the C4 suite over new images is the proof. Never touch `datomworld-c4-*` worktrees (none exist in `git worktree list` today; the C4 work seems to live in the main checkout's branches).\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:222:2. **Accidental coverage loss when deleting 317 deftests.** Mitigation: Q7 audit list in the 8f report (deleted test name, reason: tests deleted code / ported to X / replaced by Y); port the engine-level tests; reviewer refuses 8f without the list. Count today: 4574.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:227:7. **Review-round inflation.** Phases 5-7 averaged 2-4 rounds; 8c and 8f are the two slices with the most files and the most hosts. Mitigation: split 8f into two commits (Q3) so the reviewer reads the rename as moves; keep `--find-renames` diffs in the report.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:230:**Rollback story.** Every slice is a branch; `srvm-phase8` is not merged to master until 8g. Rolling back a slice is deleting its branch and re-running the predecessor's quick tier. Rolling back after master lands is a `git revert` of the one merge commit; nothing is persisted outside git (dev-only repo, no deployed stores, owner rule). The regenerated goldens and C4 manifests are recomputable from the printed intermediates in each slice report, so no golden is ever \"lost\": the old values are in git history and the new ones in the report.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:242:| 8f | 3 | 3-4 | 5-6 days + slow tier (JVM 20+ min, Node/Dart ~5 min each, C4 slow sequence hours on a laptop; use shiva/jupiter) |\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:246:Not counted: the owner's own time on Q1-Q6, and any C4-side rebase the other orchestrator needs after 8f.\ncollab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md:254:- **Q1** who edits the 10 C4 files and the two C4 manifest goldens, and the freeze window.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:130:5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), and at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track (owner decision 2026-10-12; see \"Test tiers: quick and slow\" below). G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:185:## Test tiers: quick and slow\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:187:The suite has two tiers so that slow tests run less often than quick ones\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:203:- **Cadence:** the qu